Subject: mips/mm: HIGHMEM lowmem fast paths for non-coherent DMA sync and page_address (#27)

HIGHMEM=y costs the CPU-port NIC path per packet although every NIC buffer is lowmem
(page_pool and slab never use __GFP_HIGHMEM). Measured: docs/NAT.md "HIGHMEM", #27.
- dma_sync_phys: lowmem range -> one cache op on phys_to_virt(); no pfn_to_page, per-page
  loop or kmap_atomic/kunmap_atomic (2 out-of-line calls + page_address per sync).
- page_address: inline the !PageHighMem case (lowmem_page_address); the hash lookup moves to
  page_address_hashed(). GRO, RX build_skb, skb frag paths call it per packet.
Upstreamable: both are generic (MIPS non-coherent DMA; any HASHED_PAGE_VIRTUAL arch); not sent.
---
--- a/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
+++ b/arch/mips/mm/dma-noncoherent.c
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 #include <linux/dma-direct.h>
 #include <linux/dma-map-ops.h>
 #include <linux/highmem.h>
+#include <linux/memblock.h>
+#include <linux/pfn.h>
 
 #include <asm/cache.h>
 #include <asm/cpu-type.h>
@@ -95,10 +97,21 @@
